"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdocs=self.webpackChunkdocs||[]).push([[482],{71412:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"functions":[{"name":"_listenForModels","desc":"Discovers mineable nodes and keeps the registry in step with the tag.\\n\\nSweeps `CollectionService:GetTagged(Mineables.TAG)` for nodes that already\\nexist, then connects the added/removed signals. Each new node is turned\\ninto a [MineableModelData] pair \u2014 clone, strip collision from the clone,\\nremove its tag so it isn\'t rediscovered, make the original transparent \u2014\\nand bucketed under its `MineableType`. Nodes with a missing or unknown\\ntype warn and are skipped.\\n\\nRemoval destroys the visual clone and drops the entry.","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","private":true,"source":{"line":205,"path":"src/Client/Features/Mineables/MineablesController.luau"}},{"name":"init","desc":"Bootstrap hook. Starts node discovery via\\n[MineablesController._listenForModels]. Input and rewards are wired up\\nlater, in [MineablesController.start].","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":294,"path":"src/Client/Features/Mineables/MineablesController.luau"}},{"name":"start","desc":"Bootstrap hook, run after [MineablesController.init]. Subscribes to\\n`MINEABLE_AWARD` and binds the two `ContextActionService` actions\\n(`MineableDetection`, `MineableClick`).\\n\\nThe award handler looks the granted item up under\\n`ReplicatedStorage.Assets.Resources` by `itemId`, warns and bails if there\\nis no model for it, and otherwise spawns a [DropsController] drop two\\nstuds above the award position with `tweenToCharacterOnClaim` and\\n`autoClaimOnDestruction` set \u2014 so the reward lands whether the player\\nwalks over it or not.","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":313,"path":"src/Client/Features/Mineables/MineablesController.luau"}}],"properties":[],"types":[{"name":"MineableModelAttributes","desc":"Instance attributes carried by a tagged mineable model. Set by the server;\\nthe client reads them and only ever writes `LastHitAt` (optimistically)\\nand `OriginalScale` (lazily, on first hit).","fields":[{"name":"MineableId","lua_type":"string","desc":"Server-side identity, sent with every `MINEABLE_HIT`"},{"name":"MineableType","lua_type":"string","desc":"Must be one of `Mineables.TYPES`; buckets the node in `models`"},{"name":"MaxHealth","lua_type":"number","desc":"Server-owned"},{"name":"Health","lua_type":"number","desc":"Server-owned"},{"name":"OriginalScale","lua_type":"number","desc":"Scale to return to after the hit squash"},{"name":"LastHitAt","lua_type":"number","desc":"`os.clock()` of the last registered hit"},{"name":"HitCooldown","lua_type":"number","desc":"Minimum seconds between hits on this node"}],"source":{"line":97,"path":"src/Client/Features/Mineables/MineablesController.luau"}},{"name":"MineableModelData","desc":"One mineable node, as the pair of models described in the class docs.","fields":[{"name":"model","lua_type":"Model","desc":"The tagged, invisible original. Owns collision, used for raycasts"},{"name":"visualModel","lua_type":"Model","desc":"Non-colliding clone. Owns the visuals, safe to scale and tween"}],"source":{"line":119,"path":"src/Client/Features/Mineables/MineablesController.luau"}}],"name":"MineablesController","desc":"Client half of the mining loop: finds mineable nodes by CollectionService\\ntag, handles hover and click, and dispatches hits to the server.\\n\\n### The two-model trick\\n\\nEvery tagged node ends up as a *pair*. The tagged model stays where the\\nserver put it and keeps its collision geometry for raycasts, but all of\\nits parts are made fully transparent. A clone \u2014 the `visualModel` \u2014 is\\nparented to Workspace with collision, touch and query all disabled, its\\ntag removed (so discovery doesn\'t recurse), and `ModelStreamingMode` set\\nto `Persistent`.\\n\\nThe point is that hit detection and visuals can then move independently:\\nthe visual model is free to squash on impact via `ScaleTween` without ever\\nperturbing what the raycast sees. `MineablesController.models` holds these\\npairs bucketed by `MineableType`.\\n\\n### Attributes\\n\\nNodes are configured entirely through instance attributes; see\\n[MineableModelAttributes]. `Mineables.REQUIRED_MODEL_ATTRIBUTES` is\\nvalidated on hover, and a node missing any of them warns and is ignored.\\n`Health` and `MaxHealth` are the server\'s business \u2014 the client only reads\\n`LastHitAt`, `HitCooldown`, `MineableId` and `OriginalScale`.\\n\\n`OriginalScale` is lazily captured on the first hit if absent, so the\\nsquash tween always has a scale to return to.\\n\\n### Input\\n\\nTwo `ContextActionService` bindings, both still on the legacy input path:\\n\\n* `MineableDetection` on mouse movement \u2014 raycasts from the camera, walks\\n  up to the tagged parent, validates it, and drops the hover if it is\\n  further than `Mineables.MAX_DISTANCE`. Sets the hover cursor and *sinks*\\n  the input while hovering.\\n* `MineableClick` on MouseButton1 / Touch \u2014 re-resolves the target if\\n  there is no current hover (so a fast click without a preceding\\n  move still registers), then applies two independent cooldowns before\\n  dispatching.\\n\\n### Hit dispatch and rewards\\n\\nA click that passes both cooldowns \u2014 `Mineables.PLAYER_HIT_COOLDOWN`\\nagainst the module-local `lastLocalHitAt`, and the node\'s own\\n`HitCooldown` against its `LastHitAt` attribute \u2014 writes `LastHitAt`\\nlocally for immediate feedback (the server overwrites it), dispatches\\n`MINEABLE_HIT` with the node\'s `MineableId`, emits the `MineableHit`\\nparticle at the raycast point, and squashes the visual model to 1.3x and\\nback.\\n\\nRewards come back asynchronously as `MINEABLE_AWARD`, which is subscribed\\nin [MineablesController.start] and turned into a [DropsController] drop\\nthat flies to the character and shows a `+1` popup.\\n\\nCopyright (c) 2026 firebit. All rights reserved.\\nfirebit/murder-escape - proprietary and confidential.","realm":["Client"],"source":{"line":63,"path":"src/Client/Features/Mineables/MineablesController.luau"}}')}}]);